===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|implacable}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|implācābilis}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɪmˈplækəbəl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Not able to be [[placate]]d or [[appease]]d.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Twelfth Night|act=III|scene=iv|page=269|passage=He is knight dubb'd with vnhatche'd Rapier, and on carpet conſideration, but he is a diuell in priuate [[brawl|brall]], soules and bodies hath he diuorc'd three, and his incenſement at this moment is ſo '''implacable''', that ſatisfaction can be none, but by pangs of death and ſepulcher: Hob, nob, is his word: giu't or take't.}}
# [[adamant|Adamant]]; [[immovable]].

